# Mission Control organization

Current authority: the code, then `docs/adr/` (decisions), explained by `docs/knowledge/mission-control.md`,
`lanes-and-harness.md`, `database-component.md` and the workflow concepts. The origin spec pack was deleted on 2026-11-01.

Read root AGENTS.md, the closest source AGENTS.md, and docs/knowledge/index.md.
Concepts explain implementation; they do not amend contracts or certify deployment.

One distribution imports mission_control from src/mission_control. Interfaces
call application; application uses domain and ports; adapters implement ports;
bootstrap wires dependencies. Temporal alone schedules missions; Deep Agents
performs bounded cognition. Checkpoints cannot decide semantic acceptance.

PostgreSQL owns application persistence; Temporal persistence is separate. Common
SQL lives only in packages/mission-control-db-contract (mission-db); app targets
live in deployments/<app>. Legacy schemas are never a fallback.
Application-specific knowledge services stay outside the general kernel.

Historical BellLabs specs, WPs and old guides are provenance. They cannot restore
obsolete app/, Mongo or endpoint authority. Preserve unrelated work and recovery
checkpoints. Report local proof, external blockers and unimplemented scope separately.
